{"name":"Artificial Intelligence Grey","hex":"#a1a1a1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"artificial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Man-made; made by humans; of artifice.","Insincere; fake, forced, or feigned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artificial"},{"term":"intelligence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The capacity of mind, especially to understand principles, truths, facts or meanings, acquire knowledge, and apply it to practice; the ability to comprehend and learn; the ability to process sentient experience to generate true beliefs with a justified degree of confidence.","An individual's expected relative performance in a cognitive test."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligence"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Artificial intelligence","blocks":[{"text":"Artificial intelligence (AI) is the capability of computational systems to perform tasks typically associated with human intelligence, such as learning, reasoning, problem-solving, perception, and decision-making. It is a field of research in engineering, mathematics, and computer science that develops and studies methods and software that enable machines to perceive their environment and use learning and intelligence to take actions that maximise their chances of achieving defined goals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence","wikidata":"Q11660"},{"title":"Intelligence","blocks":[{"text":"Intelligence has been defined in many ways: the capacity for abstraction, logic, understanding, self-awareness, learning, emotional knowledge, reasoning, planning, creativity, critical thinking, and problem-solving. It can be described as the ability to perceive or infer information and to retain it as knowledge to be applied to adaptive behaviors within an environment or context."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Greek_uc_psi_icon.svg/330px-Greek_uc_psi_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligence","wikidata":"Q83500"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png/500px-Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png/500px-Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In supervised learning, the training data is labelled with the expected answers, while in unsupervised learning, the model identifies patterns or structures in unlabelled data.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASupervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg/500px-Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg/1280px-Kism